{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>[The enemy] said</b> — I have seen many interpretations, and not one of them is tied to what precedes and follows it. And according to my view: its meaning is that the enemy who comes to Bashan, to the land of Israel, will thus return to his house just as one who drowns in the depths of the sea returns. And the meaning of 'said' is 'thus HaShem decreed,' as I have explained in several places."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 68, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:11.822963350Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}